IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ea-part2-continuity`
IMPORT `ea-part3-salary`
IMPORT `ea-part4-hours`

-- Employment Act 1968, Part 2 (ss 15-18A), Part 3 and Part 4 -- worked cases.

§ `Part 2 -- sections 15 to 18A`

§§ `15 -- the danger escape`

GIVEN `immediate` IS A BOOLEAN, `undertook the risk` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DangerFacts
DECIDE `danger that is` `immediate` `undertook the risk` IS
    DangerFacts WITH
        `the threat is to the employee or the employee's dependant` IS TRUE
        `the danger is immediate` IS `immediate`
        `the danger is to the person` IS TRUE
        `the danger is by violence or disease` IS TRUE
        `the employee undertook by the contract of service to run that risk` IS `undertook the risk`

#ASSERT `the employee may terminate without notice under section 15` (`danger that is` TRUE FALSE)
-- A danger that is real but not immediate is outside s 15.
#ASSERT NOT `the employee may terminate without notice under section 15` (`danger that is` FALSE FALSE)
-- And the risk the contract undertook -- the nurse, the security guard -- is
-- outside it however immediate.
#ASSERT NOT `the employee may terminate without notice under section 15` (`danger that is` TRUE TRUE)

§§ `16 -- the measure of damages, and that the contract may displace it`

-- The default measure is the payment in lieu of notice: 28 days at $200.
#ASSERT `the sum payable on breach under section 16` 200 28 EQUALS 5600
#ASSERT `the amount recoverable for breach` FALSE 0 200 28 EQUALS 5600
-- "Subject to anything in the contract of service to the contrary": unlike s 8,
-- s 16 yields to the contract in EITHER direction, including a measure less
-- favourable to the employee.
#ASSERT `the amount recoverable for breach` TRUE 100 200 28 EQUALS 100

§§ `17 -- trade union rights`

#ASSERT `the contractual restriction has no effect under section 17` (PurportedRestriction WITH `on joining a registered trade union` IS TRUE, `on participating in the activities of a registered trade union` IS FALSE, `on associating with others to organise a trade union under the Trade Unions Act 1940` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the contractual restriction has no effect under section 17` (PurportedRestriction WITH `on joining a registered trade union` IS FALSE, `on participating in the activities of a registered trade union` IS FALSE, `on associating with others to organise a trade union under the Trade Unions Act 1940` IS FALSE)

§§ `18 and 18A -- continuity`

GIVEN `statutory substitution` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `death` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `partners changed` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `undertaking transferred` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `employed in it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN EmployerChange
DECIDE `a change by` `statutory substitution` `death` `partners changed` `undertaking transferred` `employed in it` IS
    EmployerChange WITH
        `a body corporate was substituted as employer by or under written law` IS `statutory substitution`
        `the employer died and the employee was taken into the employment of the personal representatives or trustees` IS `death`
        `there was a change in the partners, personal representatives or trustees who employ the person` IS `partners changed`
        `an undertaking or part of one was transferred from one person to another` IS `undertaking transferred`
        `the employee was employed by the transferor in the undertaking or part transferred` IS `employed in it`

`no change at all` MEANS `a change by` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

#ASSERT NOT `the continuity of the period of employment is preserved` `no change at all`
#ASSERT `the continuity of the period of employment is preserved` (`a change by` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the continuity of the period of employment is preserved` (`a change by` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the continuity of the period of employment is preserved` (`a change by` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the continuity of the period of employment is preserved` (`a change by` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)

-- s 18A needs BOTH limbs: an undertaking transferred AND this employee employed
-- in the part transferred. A transfer of some other division does nothing.
#ASSERT NOT `the continuity of the period of employment is preserved` (`a change by` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the transfer does not terminate the contract of service` (`a change by` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the transfer does not terminate the contract of service` (`a change by` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the terms and conditions of service are unchanged by the transfer` (`a change by` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)

-- s 18A(5): all three heads of information, or the duty is not discharged.
#ASSERT `the transferor has discharged the section 18A(5) duty` (TransferNotice WITH `the fact, approximate date and reasons for the transfer were notified` IS TRUE, `the implications and the measures the transferor envisages were notified` IS TRUE, `the measures the transferee envisages were notified` IS TRUE, `the transferee gave the transferor the information needed` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the transferor has discharged the section 18A(5) duty` (TransferNotice WITH `the fact, approximate date and reasons for the transfer were notified` IS TRUE, `the implications and the measures the transferor envisages were notified` IS TRUE, `the measures the transferee envisages were notified` IS FALSE, `the transferee gave the transferor the information needed` IS FALSE)

§ `Part 3 -- Payment of Salary`

§§ `20 -- the salary period`

#ASSERT `the fixed salary period contravenes section 20(2)` (SalaryPeriod WITH `a salary period has been fixed by the employer` IS TRUE, `the fixed period, in months` IS 2)
#ASSERT NOT `the fixed salary period contravenes section 20(2)` (SalaryPeriod WITH `a salary period has been fixed by the employer` IS TRUE, `the fixed period, in months` IS 1)
-- s 20(3): no period fixed, so one month is deemed.
#ASSERT `the salary period, in months` (SalaryPeriod WITH `a salary period has been fixed by the employer` IS FALSE, `the fixed period, in months` IS 0) EQUALS 1

§§ `20A -- the incomplete month, and the half-day rule`

GIVEN `rate` IS A NUMBER
    , `full required` IS A NUMBER, `short required` IS A NUMBER
    , `full worked` IS A NUMBER, `short worked` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN IncompleteMonth
DECIDE `a month with` `rate` `full required` `short required` `full worked` `short worked` IS
    IncompleteMonth WITH
        `the employee is monthly-rated` IS TRUE
        `commenced employment after the first day of the month` IS TRUE
        `employment was terminated before the end of the month` IS FALSE
        `took leave of absence without pay for one or more days` IS FALSE
        `took leave of absence to perform national service under the Enlistment Act 1970` IS FALSE
        `the monthly gross rate of pay` IS `rate`
        `full days the employee is required to work in that month` IS `full required`
        `short days the employee is required to work in that month, of 5 hours or less` IS `short required`
        `full days actually worked` IS `full worked`
        `short days actually worked, of 5 hours or less` IS `short worked`

-- $2,200 a month, 22 required days, 11 worked: half the month, half the pay.
#ASSERT `the salary due for the incomplete month` (`a month with` 2200 22 0 11 0) EQUALS 1100
#ASSERT `section 20A applies` (`a month with` 2200 22 0 11 0)

-- s 20A(2): a day of 5 hours or less counts as HALF on both sides. 20 full days
-- plus 4 short days is 22 required days, not 24; working 10 full and 2 short is
-- 11 days, not 12.
#ASSERT `the days required to work, counting short days as half` (`a month with` 2200 20 4 10 2) EQUALS 22
#ASSERT `the days actually worked, counting short days as half` (`a month with` 2200 20 4 10 2) EQUALS 11
#ASSERT `the salary due for the incomplete month` (`a month with` 2200 20 4 10 2) EQUALS 1100

§§ `21 to 23 -- the payment deadlines`

#ASSERT `the number of days allowed for payment` `ordinary salary for a salary period` EQUALS 7
#ASSERT `the number of days allowed for payment` `additional payment for overtime work` EQUALS 14
#ASSERT `the number of days allowed for payment` `dismissal by the employer` EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `the number of days allowed for payment` `termination by the employee without notice` EQUALS 7
#ASSERT `the number of days allowed for payment` `termination by the employee with due notice or payment in lieu` EQUALS 0

-- The employer who dismisses has 3 days; the employee who walks out gives the
-- employer 7. Asserted as the pair.
#ASSERT `the payment was late` `dismissal by the employer` 4
#ASSERT NOT `the payment was late` `dismissal by the employer` 3
#ASSERT NOT `the payment was late` `termination by the employee without notice` 7

§§ `25 -- the manner of payment`

#ASSERT `the manner of payment satisfies section 25` (PaymentManner WITH `paid into an account with a bank in Singapore in the employee's name or jointly` IS TRUE, `paid on a working day during working hours` IS FALSE, `paid at the place of work or another place agreed between employer and employee` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `the manner of payment satisfies section 25` (PaymentManner WITH `paid into an account with a bank in Singapore in the employee's name or jointly` IS FALSE, `paid on a working day during working hours` IS TRUE, `paid at the place of work or another place agreed between employer and employee` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the manner of payment satisfies section 25` (PaymentManner WITH `paid into an account with a bank in Singapore in the employee's name or jointly` IS FALSE, `paid on a working day during working hours` IS FALSE, `paid at the place of work or another place agreed between employer and employee` IS TRUE)

§§ `26 and 27 -- what may be deducted, and consent`

`consent given and standing` MEANS Consent WITH `written consent was given` IS TRUE, `written notice of withdrawal was given before the deduction was made` IS FALSE
`consent given then withdrawn` MEANS Consent WITH `written consent was given` IS TRUE, `written notice of withdrawal was given before the deduction was made` IS TRUE
`no consent` MEANS Consent WITH `written consent was given` IS FALSE, `written notice of withdrawal was given before the deduction was made` IS FALSE

#ASSERT NOT `the deduction is authorised` `not authorised by the Act at all`
#ASSERT `the deduction is authorised` `absence from work`
#ASSERT `the deduction is authorised` `contributions under the Central Provident Fund Act 1953`

-- Deductions for absence and for CPF need no consent.
#ASSERT NOT `the deduction requires the employee's written consent` `absence from work`
#ASSERT `the deduction may lawfully be made` `absence from work` `no consent`

-- Accommodation does, and s 27(1A) lets the employee withdraw it before the
-- deduction is made.
#ASSERT `the deduction requires the employee's written consent` `house accommodation supplied by the employer`
#ASSERT `the deduction may lawfully be made` `house accommodation supplied by the employer` `consent given and standing`
#ASSERT NOT `the deduction may lawfully be made` `house accommodation supplied by the employer` `consent given then withdrawn`
#ASSERT NOT `the deduction may lawfully be made` `house accommodation supplied by the employer` `no consent`

§§ `28 to 31 -- the individual ceilings`

-- s 28(2): the deduction for absence is proportionate. Absent 2 days of 22, on
-- $2,200: $200.
#ASSERT `the maximum deduction for absence` 2200 2 22 EQUALS 200

-- s 29: three separate requirements.
GIVEN `proposed` IS A NUMBER, `loss` IS A NUMBER, `permitted` IS A BOOLEAN, `showed cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DamagesDeduction
DECIDE `a damages deduction` `proposed` `loss` `permitted` `showed cause` IS
    DamagesDeduction WITH
        `the amount of the damages or loss caused by the employee's neglect or default` IS `loss`
        `one month's wages` IS 2000
        `the amount the employer proposes to deduct` IS `proposed`
        `the Commissioner has permitted a larger deduction` IS `permitted`
        `the employee has been given an opportunity of showing cause` IS `showed cause`

-- A quarter of $2,000 is $500.
#ASSERT `the quarter-of-a-month ceiling` (`a damages deduction` 400 900 FALSE TRUE) `the proportions as the Act states them` EQUALS 500

-- Within both ceilings and cause shown: lawful.
#ASSERT `the damages deduction may be made` (`a damages deduction` 400 900 FALSE TRUE) `the proportions as the Act states them`
-- Above the quarter: barred, unless the Commissioner permits.
#ASSERT NOT `the damages deduction may be made` (`a damages deduction` 600 900 FALSE TRUE) `the proportions as the Act states them`
#ASSERT `the damages deduction may be made` (`a damages deduction` 600 900 TRUE TRUE) `the proportions as the Act states them`
-- Above the actual loss: barred even with the Commissioner's permission,
-- because the first ceiling is not one the Commissioner may lift.
#ASSERT NOT `the damages deduction may be made` (`a damages deduction` 950 900 TRUE TRUE) `the proportions as the Act states them`
-- And no opportunity to show cause: barred however small the sum.
#ASSERT NOT `the damages deduction may be made` (`a damages deduction` 10 900 FALSE FALSE) `the proportions as the Act states them`

-- s 30(2): both ceilings, the value and the quarter of the period's salary.
#ASSERT `the accommodation deductions are within section 30` 400 500 2000 `the proportions as the Act states them`
#ASSERT NOT `the accommodation deductions are within section 30` 600 1000 2000 `the proportions as the Act states them`
#ASSERT NOT `the accommodation deductions are within section 30` 400 300 2000 `the proportions as the Act states them`

-- s 31(2): advances over not more than 12 months.
#ASSERT `the advance is spread within section 31(2)` 12
#ASSERT NOT `the advance is spread within section 31(2)` 13
#ASSERT `the instalment is within the limit` 500 2000 `the proportions as the Act states them`
#ASSERT NOT `the instalment is within the limit` 501 2000 `the proportions as the Act states them`

§§ `32 -- the overall cap, and the three heads that escape it`

#ASSERT `the deduction counts towards the section 32 cap` `house accommodation supplied by the employer`
#ASSERT NOT `the deduction counts towards the section 32 cap` `absence from work`
#ASSERT NOT `the deduction counts towards the section 32 cap` `recovery of an advance, loan, unearned employment benefit or overpayment`
#ASSERT NOT `the deduction counts towards the section 32 cap` `payments to a registered cooperative society`

#ASSERT `the section 32 cap is satisfied` 1000 2000 FALSE `the proportions as the Act states them`
#ASSERT NOT `the section 32 cap is satisfied` 1001 2000 FALSE `the proportions as the Act states them`
-- s 32(2): the cap does not apply to the last salary on termination.
#ASSERT `the section 32 cap is satisfied` 1900 2000 TRUE `the proportions as the Act states them`

§§ `33 -- who gets priority`

GIVEN `workman` IS A BOOLEAN, `manager` IS A BOOLEAN, `salary` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Worker
DECIDE `a worker` `workman` `manager` `salary` IS
    Worker WITH
        `is a workman` IS `workman`
        `is employed in a managerial or an executive position` IS `manager`
        `monthly salary excluding overtime, bonus, annual wage supplement, productivity incentive and allowances` IS `salary`

#ASSERT `section 33 applies to the worker` (`a worker` TRUE FALSE 4500) `the caps as the Act states them`
#ASSERT NOT `section 33 applies to the worker` (`a worker` TRUE FALSE 4501) `the caps as the Act states them`
#ASSERT `section 33 applies to the worker` (`a worker` FALSE FALSE 2600) `the caps as the Act states them`
#ASSERT NOT `section 33 applies to the worker` (`a worker` FALSE FALSE 2601) `the caps as the Act states them`
-- A manager is outside limb (b) however little they earn, and outside (a)
-- unless also a workman.
#ASSERT NOT `section 33 applies to the worker` (`a worker` FALSE TRUE 1000) `the caps as the Act states them`

§ `Part 4 -- Rest days, hours of work`

§§ `36 -- the rest day and the shift substitution`

GIVEN `whole day` IS A BOOLEAN, `shift` IS A BOOLEAN, `substituted` IS A BOOLEAN, `before 6pm sunday` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A RestDayArrangement
DECIDE `a rest day arrangement` `whole day` `shift` `substituted` `before 6pm sunday` IS
    RestDayArrangement WITH
        `a rest day of one whole day was allowed in the week` IS `whole day`
        `the employee is engaged in shift work` IS `shift`
        `a continuous period of 30 hours was substituted` IS `substituted`
        `the substituted period commenced before 6 p.m. on a Sunday` IS `before 6pm sunday`
        `the employer determines the rest day` IS TRUE
        `a roster was prepared before the commencement of the month` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `a rest day was allowed in the week` (`a rest day arrangement` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `a rest day was allowed in the week` (`a rest day arrangement` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- The 30-hour substitution is available only to a shift worker.
#ASSERT `a rest day was allowed in the week` (`a rest day arrangement` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `a rest day was allowed in the week` (`a rest day arrangement` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 36(3): the deeming that saves a period running past the end of the week.
#ASSERT `the rest day is deemed granted within the week` (`a rest day arrangement` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the rest day is deemed granted within the week` (`a rest day arrangement` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)

§§ `37 -- the rest day payment table`

GIVEN `hours` IS A NUMBER, `own request` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A RestDayWork
DECIDE `rest day work` `hours` `own request` IS
    RestDayWork WITH
        `hours agreed as the usual hours of work per day were agreed` IS FALSE
        `the agreed usual hours of work per day` IS 0
        `the hours actually worked on the rest day` IS `hours`
        `the basic rate of pay for one day's work` IS 100
        `the hourly basic rate of pay` IS 12.5
        `the work was at the employee's own request` IS `own request`

-- No agreement, so normal hours are deemed 8.
#ASSERT `normal hours of work` (`rest day work` 4 TRUE) EQUALS 8

-- At the EMPLOYEE'S request: half a day, one day, one day plus the excess.
#ASSERT `the payment for working on the rest day` (`rest day work` 4 TRUE) EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `the payment for working on the rest day` (`rest day work` 6 TRUE) EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `the payment for working on the rest day` (`rest day work` 8 TRUE) EQUALS 100
-- 10 hours: one day's pay plus 2 hours at 1.5 x 12.50 = 100 + 37.50.
#ASSERT `the payment for working on the rest day` (`rest day work` 10 TRUE) EQUALS 137.5

-- At the EMPLOYER'S request: every band doubled.
#ASSERT `the payment for working on the rest day` (`rest day work` 4 FALSE) EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `the payment for working on the rest day` (`rest day work` 6 FALSE) EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `the payment for working on the rest day` (`rest day work` 8 FALSE) EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `the payment for working on the rest day` (`rest day work` 10 FALSE) EQUALS 237.5

-- The boundary at exactly half the normal hours: 4 of 8 is "does not exceed
-- half", so it falls in paragraph (a).
#ASSERT `the payment for working on the rest day` (`rest day work` 4.5 TRUE) EQUALS 100

§§ `38 -- hours, the provisos, and overtime`

GIVEN `shorter days` IS A BOOLEAN, `five day week` IS A BOOLEAN, `alternate weeks` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A WorkPattern
DECIDE `a pattern with` `shorter days` `five day week` `alternate weeks` IS
    WorkPattern WITH
        `by agreement, hours on one or more days of the week are less than 8` IS `shorter days`
        `by agreement, the employee works not more than 5 days a week` IS `five day week`
        `by agreement, hours in every alternate week are less than 44` IS `alternate weeks`

`the ordinary pattern` MEANS `a pattern with` FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a five day week` MEANS `a pattern with` FALSE TRUE FALSE
`alternating weeks` MEANS `a pattern with` FALSE FALSE TRUE

#ASSERT `the daily hours ceiling` `the ordinary pattern` EQUALS 8
#ASSERT `the daily hours ceiling` `a five day week` EQUALS 9
#ASSERT `the weekly hours ceiling` `the ordinary pattern` EQUALS 44
#ASSERT `the weekly hours ceiling` `alternating weeks` EQUALS 48

GIVEN `pattern` IS A WorkPattern, `day hours` IS A NUMBER, `week hours` IS A NUMBER, `consecutive` IS A NUMBER, `ot month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A HoursWorked
DECIDE `hours of` `pattern` `day hours` `week hours` `consecutive` `ot month` IS
    HoursWorked WITH
        `the pattern` IS `pattern`
        `hours worked in the day` IS `day hours`
        `hours worked in the week` IS `week hours`
        `hours worked in the continuous period of 2 weeks` IS 0
        `consecutive hours worked without a period of leisure` IS `consecutive`
        `the hourly basic rate of pay` IS 12.5
        `overtime hours worked in the month` IS `ot month`
        `a section 38(2) circumstance applies` IS FALSE

-- On the ordinary pattern, a 10-hour day is 2 hours of overtime; on a five-day
-- week it is only 1, because the ceiling moves to 9.
#ASSERT `the daily hours attracting overtime` (`hours of` `the ordinary pattern` 10 40 5 0) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the daily hours attracting overtime` (`hours of` `a five day week` 10 40 5 0) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the weekly hours attracting overtime` (`hours of` `the ordinary pattern` 8 48 5 0) EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `the weekly hours attracting overtime` (`hours of` `alternating weeks` 8 48 5 0) EQUALS 0

-- 1.5 x $12.50 x 2 hours.
#ASSERT `the overtime payment` 2 12.5 EQUALS 37.5

-- s 38(1)(a): six consecutive hours, with no proviso to raise it.
#ASSERT `section 38(1)(a) was contravened` (`hours of` `the ordinary pattern` 8 40 7 0)
#ASSERT NOT `section 38(1)(a) was contravened` (`hours of` `the ordinary pattern` 8 40 6 0)

-- s 38(5): 72 overtime hours a month.
#ASSERT `section 38(5) was contravened` (`hours of` `the ordinary pattern` 8 40 5 73)
#ASSERT NOT `section 38(5) was contravened` (`hours of` `the ordinary pattern` 8 40 5 72)

-- s 38(8): the 12-hour absolute ceiling, excepted only by s 38(2)(a) to (e).
-- The economic ground in s 38(2)(f) does NOT lift it.
#ASSERT `section 38(8) was contravened` (`hours of` `the ordinary pattern` 13 40 5 0) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 38(8) was contravened` (`hours of` `the ordinary pattern` 13 40 5 0) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 38(8) was contravened` (`hours of` `the ordinary pattern` 12 40 5 0) FALSE

§§ `40 -- shift workers and the three-week average`

GIVEN `regular shift` IS A BOOLEAN, `consented` IS A BOOLEAN, `explained` IS A BOOLEAN, `hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A ShiftArrangement
DECIDE `a shift arrangement` `regular shift` `consented` `explained` `hours` IS
    ShiftArrangement WITH
        `engaged under the contract of service in regular shift work` IS `regular shift`
        `consented in writing to work the section 40 hours` IS `consented`
        `sections 38 and 40 were explained to the employee before consent` IS `explained`
        `total hours worked over the continuous period of 3 weeks` IS `hours`

-- s 40(2): consent without the explanation is not valid consent.
#ASSERT `the consent is valid under section 40(2)` (`a shift arrangement` FALSE TRUE TRUE 120)
#ASSERT NOT `the consent is valid under section 40(2)` (`a shift arrangement` FALSE TRUE FALSE 120)
#ASSERT NOT `section 40 applies to the employee` (`a shift arrangement` FALSE TRUE FALSE 120)
-- A regular shift worker is within s 40 without consenting to anything.
#ASSERT `section 40 applies to the employee` (`a shift arrangement` TRUE FALSE FALSE 120)

-- 44 hours a week averaged over 3 weeks is 132.
#ASSERT NOT `the section 40(1) average was exceeded` (`a shift arrangement` TRUE FALSE FALSE 132)
#ASSERT `the section 40(1) average was exceeded` (`a shift arrangement` TRUE FALSE FALSE 133)

§§ `45 and 46 -- the qualifying periods`

GIVEN `years` IS A NUMBER, `redundancy` IS A BOOLEAN, `ceased` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A ServiceForBenefits
DECIDE `service for benefits` `years` `redundancy` `ceased` IS
    ServiceForBenefits WITH
        `years of continuous service with the employer` IS `years`
        `dismissed on the ground of redundancy or by reason of a reorganisation` IS `redundancy`
        `the service has ceased` IS `ceased`

#ASSERT `section 45 bars any retrenchment benefit` (`service for benefits` 1.5 TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `section 45 bars any retrenchment benefit` (`service for benefits` 2 TRUE TRUE)
-- The bar bites only on a redundancy dismissal.
#ASSERT NOT `section 45 bars any retrenchment benefit` (`service for benefits` 1 FALSE TRUE)

#ASSERT `section 46 bars any retirement benefit other than CPF sums` (`service for benefits` 4 FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `section 46 bars any retirement benefit other than CPF sums` (`service for benefits` 5 FALSE TRUE)
